    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0716" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg636"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 531.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that the commanding
                    officer of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Machias</hi> telegraphed to the
                    Navy Department, under date of the 13th instant, that the blockade of Cape
                    Haitien had been admitted to be ineffective by Admiral Killick and had been
                    abandoned.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
